              ]
            }
          ],
          "FACILITY": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": {
                "facility": [
                  "LINAC"
                ],
                "institute": "1USALAS"
              },
              "free_text": [
                " The Weapons Neutron Research (WNR)",
                "facility of the Los Alamos Neutron Science Center",
                " (LANSCE)."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "INC-SOURCE": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": {
                "incident_source": [
                  "SPALL"
                ],
                "reaction": null
              },
              "free_text": [
                " The LANSCE linear accelerator provided a",
                "pulsed beam of 800 MeV protons impinging on a",
                "tungsten target at WNR. Spallation reactions were",
                "generated and produced a white neutron source, with",
                "neutron energies ranging from below 1 MeV to about",
                "700 MeV."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "DETECTOR": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": [
                "FISCH",
                "SCIN"
              ],
              "free_text": [
                " A fission chamber containing a stack of",
                "22 high-purity 235U samples electrodeposited on",
                "aluminum backing by the Target Preparation Laboratory",
                "from the European Commission Joint Research Center of",
                "Geel, Belgium was placed in the neutron beam. The",
                "chamber was filled with CF4 gas at a pressure of 890",
                "mbar. The fission chamber was surrounded by the 54",
                "EJ-309 liquid scintillators from the Chi-Nu array.",
                "The detectors are 17.78 cm diameter cylindrical cells,",
                "5 cm thick, equipped with a light guide and a",
                "photomultiplier tube."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "SAMPLE": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": {
                "nuclide": "92-U-235",
                "field_identifier": "ENR",
                "value": 0.999
              },
              "free_text": [
                " Each sample with an isotopic",
                "purity above 99.9% had a mass of 2.5 mg, totalizing",
                "55 mg of 235U. The samples and their aluminum backing",
                "were used as cathodes with 11 anodes to form a stack",
                "of ionization chambers."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "METHOD": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": [
                "TOF"
              ],
              "free_text": [
                " The neutron beam was produced by a pulsed",
                "proton beam impinging on a tungsten spallation",
                "target. The experiment took place on 4FP15L, the 15.",
                "left flight path, and was placed 21.5 m away from the",
                "spallation production target. The double",
                "time-of-flight technique was used at the Los Alamos",
                "Neutron Science Center to measure incoming and prompt",
                "fission neutron energies. The data were measured",
                "relative to the very well-known 252Cf(sf) prompt",
                "fission neutron spectrum (PFNS) and nu prompt Cf. The",
                "neutron detection efficiency was calibrated using the",
                "well-known 252Cf(sf) PFNS, normalized to its",
                "evaluated nubar, and the PFNS in the 235U(n,f)",
                "reaction were reconstructed as a function of the",
                "incoming neutron energy."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "ERR-ANALYS": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": {
                "heading": "ERR-S",
                "minimum_value": null,
                "maximum_value": null,
                "correlation_property": null
              },
              "free_text": [
                " Statistical uncertainties."
              ]
            }
          ],
          "CORRECTION": [
            {
              "pointer": "",
              "coded_information": null,
              "free_text": [
                "- Low energy extrapolation and integration correction.",
                "- A correction that takes into account the angular",
                "distribution of the neutrons over the full angular",
                "range.",
                "- Wraparound correction: The highest fraction of",
                "wraparound was obtained at the lowest incoming",
                "neutron energies, where it could reach up to 5%,",
                "while the correction needed remains of the order of 1%.",
                "- A beam leakage correction was needed because of",
                "an issue with the LANSCE proton accelerator.",
                "- Dead-time correction.",
                "- Simulations of the setup are performed to correct two",
                " final effects on the data.",
                "a) First, the time resolution was 0.723 ns and 1.0 ns",
                "for the reference 252Cf(sf) PFN measurement and for",
                "the 235U(n,f) measurement, respectively. Therefore",
                "the energy resolution was not the same in both",
                "measurements.",
                "b) Second, while a large part of neutron scattering was",
                " removed during the analysis,some scattered neutrons",
                "still remained within the authors neutron selection."
              ]
            }
          ],
